# prompt: window smashing, glass shards falling
# tags: glass, break, smash, shatter
# Two grain fields at `bend 1`, which is the ice-and-glass end of the range: a
# dense one for the sheet letting go and a slow, wide one starting 380 ms later
# for the pieces reaching the floor. The gap between them is the fall, and it
# is the only thing here that gives the window a height.
sound "glass break" 900ms impact
  smash: noise white >> hp ~3000Hz[1500..7000] | gain 0.32 attack 0ms decay 60ms
  ring: modal glass ~2600Hz[1200..5500] Q140 | gain 0.2 decay 400ms
  shards: grains ~5000Hz[2500..9000] rate ~130[60..320] width 4ms spread 2.5 bend 1 | gain 0.28 decay 500ms delay 30ms
  fall: grains ~3600Hz[1800..7000] rate 30 width 8ms spread 2 bend 1 | gain 0.16 attack 40ms decay 400ms delay 380ms
